      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(setup): offer native Windows and WSL gateway modes",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- make native Windows the recommended onboarding path while preserving the existing WSL 2 and connect-existing choices\n- install the native CLI into an app-owned LocalAppData prefix and run an isolated profile/Scheduled Task without changing a user's global CLI or default profile\n- make native/WSL switching, rollback, repair, and uninstall ownership-aware so inactive or user-managed runtimes are preserved\n- complete the gateway wizard without trying to launch a terminal UI, follow native wizard logs across partial writes/rotation, and document both runtime modes\n\nBuilds on the onboarding redesign from #925.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Windows 11 ARM64 VM: full Release solution rebuild, 0 warnings / 0 errors\n- SetupEngine: 553 passed\n- Shared: 2,703 passed, 31 skipped\n- Tray: 1,596 passed\n- Connection: 399 passed\n- WinNode CLI: 126 passed\n- Functional UI: 10 passed\n- WinUI: 78 passed on ARM64\n- ARM64 self-contained publish plus release native-dependency policy: passed\n- fresh native E2E: official CLI install, random isolated profile/port, HTTP 200 health, operator/node pairing, gateway wizard completion, tray ready, and clean uninstall\n- post-uninstall probe: isolated profile/task absent; pre-existing global CLI path and `2026.6.11` version unchanged\n- structured autoreview: clean\n\nThe Parallels validation VM can run WSL 1 but cannot provide the nested virtualization required for WSL 2, so a fresh WSL 2 provisioning run is not claimed here. The WSL choice/review path and runtime-selection/switching behavior remain covered by the setup test suite and existing CI E2E lane.\n\n## Native setup reliability & WSL-parity follow-up (bc0077e4)\n\nFollow-up pass to make native Windows setup as fast, deterministic, and non-blocking as the WSL path, without weakening its Windows-specific repair semantics:\n\n- **Wizard** — give note/acknowledge steps the slow timeout ceiling so the finalize \"Security\" note ack survives the gateway's shell-completion work instead of timing out and stranding setup on the disclaimer screen.\n- **Install** — skip the native CLI reinstall when the app-owned launcher already matches the pinned version (probes only the managed launcher; any mismatch or failure falls through to a full install).\n- **Configure** — apply gateway config in one `config set --batch-file` instead of per-key CLI calls; the auth token stays in a temp file (never on argv), stale temp files are swept, and the file is always deleted in `finally`.\n- **Start** — wait for the install-launched Scheduled Task via `/healthz` polling and fail terminal on timeout instead of issuing a destructive `gateway start`; verify ownership fail-closed on the identity signals the real `gateway status --json` reports (port, `Scheduled Task` label, `OPENCLAW_PROFILE`, profile-state-dir `sourcePath`).\n- **Installer** — apply the PowerShell 5 SQLite-probe quoting workaround only when the probe is present; otherwise proceed and surface a warning (the installer script is fetched live/unpinned).\n- **Reinstall** — reset the app-owned native profile on clean runs to clear stale device/token state.\n- **Perf** — sample CPU usage via `GetSystemTimes` instead of a synchronous `PerformanceCounter` first-touch that stalled post-setup node connect.\n- Removed superseded device-token finalization helpers and past-approach comments.\n\n### Validation (Debug, ARM64)\n\n- `build.ps1`: all 5 projects, 0 warnings / 0 errors\n- SetupEngine: 568 passed\n- Shared: 2,732 passed, 31 skipped\n- Tray: 1,681 passed\n- Dual-model rubber-duck review (GPT-5.5 + Opus) plus a focused re-review of the fixes. The re-review caught a false-negative in the first ownership fix (it required `OPENCLAW_WINDOWS_TASK_NAME`, which the live status filters out of `service.command.environment`); corrected to the reliably-present identity signals and confirmed against a live managed gateway's `gateway status --json`.\n\nBroader Release-matrix suites (Connection, WinNode CLI, WinUI, Functional UI, publish policy) and the fresh native E2E from the verification above are unaffected by this pass and were not re-run here; CI covers them.",
        "branch": "codex/native-wsl-onboarding",
